{
 "id": "muse",
 "name": "Moog Muse",
 "transport": "moog",
 "source": "Moog Music, 'Muse Firmware V1.4 Release Notes (Read Me).pdf' (May 2025) -- Appendix A: MIDI CC (the only published parameter map, introduced in fw 1.1.0: 'MIDI CC map implemented'), MIDI section (program change send/receive, SEQ PGM CHNG CHANNEL); in https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/Moog/Muse/Muse%20Firmware%20V1.4.zip. Muse User's Manual v1.4.0 (https://cdn.inmusicbrands.com/Moog/Muse/Muse_Manual-1.4.0.pdf) pp.109-110 MIDI settings (KEYBOARD/LHC MIDI OUT CHANNEL, MULTI MODE, MIDI IN CHANNEL, MULTI IN B CHANNEL, SEND/RECIEVE CC, SEND/RECIEVE PGM CHNG with 'MSB is 0, LSB is 1-16 (BANK), PC is 1-16 (PATCH)'), KNOB MODE p.109, DISK MODE library p.112; panel drawing p.13. Moog forum 'Editor / VST for Moog Muse' (Derek_Cook, 2 Dec 2025: Moog support confirmed 'there is no SYSEX mode in the Muse MIDI implementation'). Electra One community '[Preset] Moog Muse' (NewIgnis, May 2026: 'controls only one Timbre; but performs Program Changes'; 'the Muse doesn't allow patch parsing'). pencilresearch/midi Moog/Muse.csv (midi.guide/d/moog/muse) cross-checked -- its envelope rows 79-89 are mislabelled, official chart used.",
 "gapMs": 1,
 "defaultChannel": 1,
 "timbres": {
  "count": 2,
  "label": "timbre",
  "names": [
   "A",
   "B"
  ],
  "note": "Bi-timbral. The CC map has no timbre field: per-timbre addressing is by MIDI channel in MULTI MODE (A = MIDI IN CHANNEL, B = MULTI IN B CHANNEL) -- see uncertain."
 },
 "driverNotes": "NEW transport 'moog' (shared with devices/moogone.json; no driver yet). For the Muse it is plain 7-bit Control Change on two channels -- no NRPN, no SysEx. (1) CHANNELS: chA = the editor channel (= Muse MIDI IN CHANNEL = KEYBOARD MIDI OUT CHANNEL); chB = a per-device pref 'timbreBChannel' (default chA + 1, 1-16) = Muse MULTI IN B CHANNEL. (2) SEND (sendParam): wire = p.wire ? p.wire[v - p.min] : v (0-127); ch = p.timbre === 'b' ? chB : chA (globals, timbre null, go on chA); midi.cc(ch, p.cc, wire). p.wire = lower bound of each option's band from the chart (switches 0 / 64; 0-24/25-49/... waveforms; 0-42/43-84/85-127 three-way; 0-31/32-63/64-95/96-127 four-way). (3) sendPatch(values): CC burst (85 per timbre + 13 global, skipping the 4 notInPatch performance controllers) -- 183 CCs, ~550 bytes, instant. (4) DECODE (decode ev): ev.type === 'cc'. On chB -> timbre b params by cc. On chA -> timbre-null params by cc, else the timbre the editor is showing (read the layout's shared 'timbre' select; default a) -- the Muse sends panel moves as CCs on KEYBOARD MIDI OUT CHANNEL with nothing that says which timbre was being edited. Enum decode: option = last i with p.wire[i] <= value. Ignore CC1/11/64 echoes of the performance controls unless shown. (5) programChange(bi, prog): CC0 = 0, CC32 = bank.lsb, PC = prog on chA (the existing selectProgram with {msb:0, lsb}). Needs RECIEVE PGM CHNG = ON. Incoming PCs (SEND PGM CHNG, default ON) arrive when the player picks a patch -> ev.type 'program' -> mark the editor's values stale. (6) requestPatch / requestProgram / writeProgram / names: impossible (no SysEx at all, per Moog support) -> throw 'Muse has no MIDI patch dump (save on the synth; back up via DISK MODE)'. (7) probe(): nothing answers; return true when the output port is open, or 'heard' once any CC/PC arrives. (8) midi.js note: receiveCC treats CC6/38/98/99 as NRPN parts -- the Muse map uses none of them, so nothing is lost.",
 "capabilities": {
  "canRead": false,
  "canBackup": false,
  "canStore": false,
  "followsPanel": "partial",
  "sendWholePatch": "CC burst of the 183 patch params (85 per timbre x 2 + 13 global), 7-bit",
  "note": "Send-only. Panel-follow is partial: only the 102 CC-mapped controls transmit (SEND CC = ON, the default), 7-bit, and a received CC can't say which timbre the player was editing. No SysEx -> no reading the current sound, no names, no MIDI backup/store. Backup is DISK MODE (hold SELECT at power-on, USB-B shows a MOOG_MUSE drive: library/bankNN/patchNN/<name>.mmp, plain-text libconfig-style files) -- a possible future file import/export path, not MIDI."
 },
 "setup": [
  "Firmware: MENU > VERSION. Needs 1.1.0+ for the CC map and 1.4.0+ (May 2025) for program change send/receive; use 1.4.",
  "MIDI (PROGRAMMER) > RECIEVE CC = ON (default OFF -- nothing the editor sends does anything until this is on).",
  "MIDI > SEND CC = ON (default) so knob moves come back to the editor.",
  "MIDI > MIDI IN CHANNEL = the editor channel; KEYBOARD MIDI OUT CHANNEL = the same channel.",
  "MIDI > MULTI MODE = ON (default) and MULTI IN B CHANNEL = editor channel + 1 (must differ from MIDI IN CHANNEL -- 1.4 refuses a collision). Timbre B edits go there.",
  "MIDI > RECIEVE PGM CHNG = ON (default OFF) for patch select from the editor; SEND PGM CHNG = ON (default) so patch changes on the synth are noticed.",
  "MENU > KNOB MODE: any; ABSOLUTE (default) means touching a knob jumps the value away from what the editor last sent.",
  "Cable both ways: USB-B (class-compliant; Windows driver 'Install Moog Music Muse 1.0.1.exe') or DIN IN + OUT."
 ],
