 "uncertain": [
  "Per-timbre CC addressing is not documented. The MULTI MODE text says 'messages at MIDI CHANNEL IN will control TIMBRE A ... TIMBRE B ... via messages at MULTI IN B CHANNEL' -- read here as covering CCs as well as notes. It may instead be that CCs only ever hit the timbre selected on the panel (Timbre Volume is described as 'for the currently active timbre'), and the Electra One preset author notes his preset 'controls only one Timbre'. First hardware test: move a B-channel CC and watch which timbre changes; if it's always the panel timbre, drop the b* params and tell the user to pick the timbre on the synth.",
  "Which timbre a transmitted panel CC belongs to is not encoded; assumed to be the panel-selected timbre.",
  "Bank select: manual prints 'LSB is 1-16 ... PC is 1-16'. Assumed 1-based display of 0-15; if bank 1 doesn't answer to LSB 0, use lsb 1-16 (and PC 1-16 would mean prog+1, unlikely).",
  "CC 33/34/36/37/40/41/43/66 are panel buttons (mod-osc routing, PAN, HIGH PASS) but the chart gives them a plain 0-127 range, not the '0-63 off / 64-127 on' used for other switches. Modelled as 0-127 as printed; probably on/off at 64.",
  "Mod Osc Waveform: chart prints SQUARE as '5-99' (typo) -- read as 75-99.",
  "Arpeggiator / Sequencer Clock Div, Clock Tempo, LFO rates: 0-127 sweeps with no published band tables or units.",
  "Filter 1 'High Pass' (CC66) and Filter 1 Cutoff 'spacing' (cutoff becomes spacing when LINK FILTERS is on) -- CC behaviour in linked mode not stated.",
  "Master MAIN OUT / HEADPHONES volume, mod map (16 slots per timbre), chord memory, voice count/split/stack, envelope curves and MORE-menu params, global mod (1.4) and sequencer steps have no CCs: the editor can't touch them.",
  "No NRPN / 14-bit anywhere in the 1.1-1.4 docs; CCs stepping is coarse on filter cutoff (128 steps).",
  "pencilresearch/midi (midi.guide) Muse.csv has the envelope CCs shifted (80 = Sustain, 81 = Delay, no Decay); the official chart (79 A, 80 D, 81 S, 82 R; 86-89 VCA A/D/S/R) is used."
 ]
